              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, justice Gorsuch posed a hypothetical about whether a beneficiary could sue for a clean trustee\u2019s actions affecting a dirty plan."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 44,
              "start": 44
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor clarified that the petitioners are seeking a payment to the plan, not a distribution to themselves."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch asked whether Congress could create a property interest for every beneficiary."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
            "evidence_ids": [
